    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Correlation and Regression Explorations\"\ndate: 03/May/2023\ndate-modified: today\nformat: html\n---\n\n## {{< iconify noto-v1 package >}} Setting up R Packages\n\n---\n# Course-wide knitr / Quarto defaults.\n# Pages should include this file and then load only the packages that lesson needs.\nknitr:\n  opts_chunk:\n    echo: true\n    warning: false\n    message: false\n    fig-align: center\n    fig-width: 6\n    fig-asp: 0.618\n    dpi: 96\n    out-width: \"75%\"\n    # ragg is fine for points/lines; fonts are registered with systemfonts below\n    # so ggrepel can see the same families. Do not pair ragg with showtext-only fonts.\n    dev: \"ragg_png\"\n---\n\n\n::: {.cell layout-align=\"center\"}\n\n:::\n\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell layout-align=\"center\"}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(tidyverse)\nlibrary(mosaic)\nlibrary(broom)\nlibrary(ggformula)\n```\n:::\n\n\n## Intro\n\nI will work through and \"unify\" at least two things:\n\n- Hadley Wickham's chapter on modelling and his analysis of the linear\n  model for the diamonds dataset\n- The diagnostic aspects of Linear Regression as detailed in Crawley's\n  book\n\n## Explorations into Diagnostic Plots\n\nLet us create dependent y\\* variables with different sorts of errors:\n\n\n::: {.cell layout-align=\"center\"}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nx <- 0:300\nen <- rnorm(301, mean = 0, sd = 5)\neu <- (runif(n = 301) - 0.5) * 20\neb <- rnbinom(n = 301, prob = 0.3, size = 2)\neg <- rgamma(n = 301, shape = 1, rate = 1 / x)\nyn <- x + 10 + en\nyu <- x + 10 + eu\nyb <- x + 10 + eb\nyg <- x + 10 + eg\ndata <- tibble(x, yn, yu, yb, yg)\ndata\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<div data-pagedtable=\"false\">\n  <script data-pagedtable-source type=\"application/json\">\n{\"columns\":[{\"label\":[\"x\"],\"name\":[1],\"type\":[\"int\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"yn\"],\"name\":[2],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"yu\"],\"name\":[3],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\"